  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **In The Midnight Hour** (1 other source): Contains a Saint Stephen jam [1]\n- **Dark Star** (1 review): The Main Ten theme appears early, before the verse, and the jam fades into drums rather than building to a peak into verse two [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **You Don't Love Me**: back after 265 archived shows (1443 days); rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **Walking The Dog**: rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1970-11-13.179403.sbd.cassidy.minches.miller.t.flac1648** (recommended): soundboard; 15 songs; 112 min; rated 1.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: The tape is horribly degraded and ragged; Charlie Miller's restoration made it listenable enough to hear the show; Sound is unlistenable until the middle of Casey Jones, with heavy tape bleed-through; making it listenable took a lot of work [1][4]\n- **gd1970-11-13.179402.sbd.cassidy.minches.miller.flac2496**: soundboard; 15 songs; 112 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Describes the Dark Star as swinging between quiet, noisy and rowdy passages [3]\n- Jamming on R&B material was a late-1970 emphasis, heard in the Not Fade Away and Goin' Down the Road sandwich, Midnight Hour and Good Lovin' [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1970-11-13.179403.sbd.cassidy.minches.miller.t.flac1648**: taped by Peter S. Kimble; transferred by Transferred by David Minches Mastered by Charlie Miller  September 28, 2026; source: SBD (mono) > Master Reel (3.75ips) [1]. Also: Tapes came from Martin Cassidy; tape flips occur in Midnight Hour and Drums [1]\n- **gd1970-11-13.179402.sbd.cassidy.minches.miller.flac2496**: taped by Peter S. Kimble; transferred by Transferred by David Minches Mastered by Charlie Miller  September 28, 2026; source: SBD (mono) > Master Reel (3.75ips) [2]",
